<title>UK: C&amp;W names C&amp;W Communications finance director.</title>
<headline>C&amp;W names C&amp;W Communications finance director.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British telecommunications group Cable &amp; Wireless Plc said on Wednesday it had appointed Nicholas Mearing-Smith as finance director of Cable &amp; Wireless Communications Plc, which will be the UK's biggest cable firm.</p>
<p>C&amp;W said Mearing-Smith, 46, will continue as chief financial officer and executive director of NYNEX CableComms Group Plc for the time being.</p>
<p>Graham Wallace was recently named chief executive of C&amp;W Communications, which is being formed by the merger of C&amp;W's Mercury unit, Nynex Corp's NYNEX CableComms Group, Bell Cablemedia Plc and Videotron Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
